<div class="doc-grid">
<section class="panel"><h2>Tech Stack</h2><ul><li>PHP for server-side pages and Activity Management operations</li><li>MySQL for persistent activity data</li><li>HTML/CSS for the interface</li><li>Vanilla JavaScript for the browser runner and visualizer</li><li>XAMPP for Apache + MySQL local hosting</li></ul></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>How Execution Works</h2><p>Each activity stores a small JavaScript operation in MySQL. The activity page sends user input to a browser-side function, executes the stored operation, and displays the result. No separate compiler is required.</p><p>The included activities use simple JavaScript snippets intended for this educational project.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Installation</h2><ol><li>Install XAMPP and start Apache and MySQL.</li><li>Copy this project folder to <code>C:/xampp/htdocs/</code>.</li><li>Open phpMyAdmin and import <code>database.sql</code>.</li><li>Visit <code>http://localhost/data_structures_activity_lab/</code>.</li><li>Log in as an admin to manage activities, or register/log in as a user to view activities.</li></ol></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Account Access</h2><ul><li>Admin accounts can add, edit, and delete activities.</li><li>User accounts can log in, log out, browse activities, open the reference PDFs, and run activities.</li><li>New registrations are always created as User accounts.</li><li>Default admin login: <code>admin</code> / <code>Admin@123</code>.</li><li>Default user login: <code>user</code> / <code>User@123</code>.</li></ul></section><section class="panel"><h2>Known Limitations</h2><ul><li>The runner executes JavaScript activities, not arbitrary PHP/C/C++/Java source code.</li><li>The visualizer is conceptual and focuses on node sequence rather than a full pointer-memory simulation.</li><li>Change the database credentials in <code>config.php</code> if your XAMPP MySQL setup differs.</li></ul></section><section class="panel"><h2>Supplied Reference PDFs</h2><p><a class="btn" target="_blank" href="resources/singly_linked_list.pdf">Singly Linked List PDF</a> <a class="btn" target="_blank" href="resources/doubly_linked_list.pdf">Doubly Linked List PDF</a> <a class="btn" target="_blank" href="resources/circular_linked_list.pdf">Circular Linked List PDF</a></p></section>
